        "content": "TRACEABILITY_JSON={\"status\":\"READY\",\"unresolved\":[],\"undefined_symbols\":[],\"requirements_mapped\":[\"lotti interi -> x_i variabile intera non negativa\",\"costo fisso di setup -> termine -f_i y_i nell'obiettivo\",\"lotto minimo e domanda massima -> L_i y_i <= x_i <= U_i y_i\",\"90 ore-macchina -> somma_i a_i x_i <= 90\",\"100 ore di lavoro -> somma_i h_i x_i <= 100\",\"almeno due articoli diversi -> somma_i y_i >= 2\",\"margine totale netto -> max somma_i (p_i x_i-f_i y_i)\"]}\n\n## Insiemi, parametri e variabili decisionali\n\n### Insieme\n\n\\[\nI=\\{A,B,C,D\\}\n\\]\n\nè l’insieme degli articoli.\n\n### Parametri\n\nPer ogni \\(i\\in I\\):\n\n- \\(p_i\\): margine unitario;\n- \\(f_i\\): costo fisso di setup;\n- \\(a_i\\): ore-macchina per unità;\n- \\(h_i\\): ore di lavoro per unità;\n- \\(L_i\\): lotto minimo;\n- \\(U_i\\): domanda massima.\n\nI valori sono:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|rrrr}\ni & A & B & C & D\\\\ \\hline\np_i & 42 & 36 & 50 & 31\\\\\nf_i & 80 & 65 & 90 & 50\\\\\na_i & 3 & 2 & 4 & 1\\\\\nh_i & 2 & 3 & 2 & 2\\\\\nL_i & 4 & 5 & 3 & 6\\\\\nU_i & 20 & 25 & 16 & 30\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nCapacità disponibili:\n\n\\[\nM=90 \\quad\\text{ore-macchina},\\qquad H=100 \\quad\\text{ore di lavoro}.\n\\]\n\n### Variabili decisionali\n\nPer ogni \\(i\\in I\\):\n\n\\[\nx_i\\in\\mathbb{Z}_{+}\n\\]\n\nnumero intero di unità prodotte dell’articolo \\(i\\);\n\n\\[\ny_i\\in\\{0,1\\}\n\\]\n\nvale \\(1\\) se l’articolo \\(i\\) viene avviato e prodotto, \\(0\\) altrimenti.\n\n## Formulazione matematica completa\n\n\\[\n\\max \\quad z=\\sum_{i\\in I}\\left(p_i x_i-f_i y_i\\right)\n\\]\n\nsoggetta a:\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{i\\in I} a_i x_i\\leq 90\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{i\\in I} h_i x_i\\leq 100\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_i\\geq L_i y_i \\qquad \\forall i\\in I\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_i\\leq U_i y_i \\qquad \\forall i\\in I\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{i\\in I}y_i\\geq 2\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx_i\\in\\mathbb{Z}_{+},\\qquad y_i\\in\\{0,1\\}\n\\qquad \\forall i\\in I.\n\\]\n\nIn forma numerica, la funzione obiettivo è:\n\n\\[\n\\max\\;\n42x_A+36x_B+50x_C+31x_D\n-80y_A-65y_B-90y_C-50y_D.\n\\]\n\nI vincoli di capacità sono:\n\n\\[\n3x_A+2x_B+4x_C+x_D\\leq 90,\n\\]\n\n\\[\n2x_A+3x_B+2x_C+2x_D\\leq 100.\n\\]\n\n## Codice Python con Gurobi\n\n```python\nimport json\nimport gurobipy as gp\nfrom gurobipy import GRB\n\nproducts = [\"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\"]\n\nmargin = {\"A\": 42, \"B\": 36, \"C\": 50, \"D\": 31}\nsetup = {\"A\": 80, \"B\": 65, \"C\": 90, \"D\": 50}\nmachine_hours = {\"A\": 3, \"B\": 2, \"C\": 4, \"D\": 1}\nlabor_hours = {\"A\": 2, \"B\": 3, \"C\": 2, \"D\": 2}\nminimum_lot = {\"A\": 4, \"B\": 5, \"C\": 3, \"D\": 6}\nmaximum_demand = {\"A\": 20, \"B\": 25, \"C\": 16, \"D\": 30}\n\nmachine_capacity = 90\nlabor_capacity = 100\n\nmodel = gp.Model(\"production_with_setup\")\nmodel.Params.OutputFlag = 0\n\nx = {\n    i: model.addVar(\n        lb=0,\n        ub=maximum_demand[i],\n        vtype=GRB.INTEGER,\n        name=f\"x_{i}\"\n    )\n    for i in products\n}\n\ny = {\n    i: model.addVar(\n        vtype=GRB.BINARY,\n        name=f\"y_{i}\"\n    )\n    for i in products\n}\n\nmodel.setObjective(\n    gp.quicksum(margin[i] * x[i] - setup[i] * y[i] for i in products),\n    GRB.MAXIMIZE\n)\n\nmodel.addConstr(\n    gp.quicksum(machine_hours[i] * x[i] for i in products)\n    <= machine_capacity,\n    name=\"machine_capacity\"\n)\n\nmodel.addConstr(\n    gp.quicksum(labor_hours[i] * x[i] for i in products)\n    <= labor_capacity,\n    name=\"labor_capacity\"\n)\n\nfor i in products:\n    model.addConstr(\n        x[i] >= minimum_lot[i] * y[i],\n        name=f\"minimum_lot_{i}\"\n    )\n    model.addConstr(\n        x[i] <= maximum_demand[i] * y[i],\n        name=f\"maximum_demand_{i}\"\n    )\n\nmodel.addConstr(\n    gp.quicksum(y[i] for i in products) >= 2,\n    name=\"minimum_number_of_products\"\n)\n\nmodel.optimize()\n\nstatus_names = {\n    GRB.LOADED: \"LOADED\",\n    GRB.OPTIMAL: \"OPTIMAL\",\n    GRB.INFEASIBLE: \"INFEASIBLE\",\n    GRB.INF_OR_UNBD: \"INF_OR_UNBD\",\n    GRB.UNBOUNDED: \"UNBOUNDED\",\n    GRB.CUTOFF: \"CUTOFF\",\n    GRB.ITERATION_LIMIT: \"ITERATION_LIMIT\",\n    GRB.NODE_LIMIT: \"NODE_LIMIT\",\n    GRB.TIME_LIMIT: \"TIME_LIMIT\",\n    GRB.SOLUTION_LIMIT: \"SOLUTION_LIMIT\",\n    GRB.INTERRUPTED: \"INTERRUPTED\",\n    GRB.NUMERIC: \"NUMERIC\",\n    GRB.SUBOPTIMAL: \"SUBOPTIMAL\",\n    GRB.INPROGRESS: \"INPROGRESS\",\n    GRB.USER_OBJ_LIMIT: \"USER_OBJ_LIMIT\"\n}\n\nsolver_status = status_names.get(model.Status, f\"STATUS_{model.Status}\")\n\nif model.Status == GRB.OPTIMAL:\n    def clean(value):\n        value = float(value)\n        if abs(value) < 1e-9:\n            return 0.0\n        nearest_integer = round(value)\n        if abs(value - nearest_integer) < 1e-9:\n            return float(nearest_integer)\n        return float(round(value, 10))\n\n    variable_values = {}\n    for i in products:\n        variable_values[f\"x_{i}\"] = clean(x[i].X)\n    for i in products:\n        variable_values[f\"y_{i}\"] = clean(y[i].X)\n\n    result = {\n        \"status\": solver_status,\n        \"objective\": clean(model.ObjVal),\n        \"variables\": variable_values\n    }\nelse:\n    result = {\n        \"status\": solver_status,\n        \"objective\": None,\n        \"variables\": {}\n    }\n\nprint(\"SOLUTION_JSON=\" + json.dumps(result, separators=(\",\", \":\")))\n```\n\n## Sintesi della soluzione\n\nLo stato è **OPTIMAL** e il margine netto massimo è:\n\n\\[\nz^*=1640.\n\\]\n\nLe decisioni non nulle sono:\n\n\\[\nx_A=20,\\quad y_A=1,\\qquad x_D=30,\\quad y_D=1.\n\\]\n\nQuesta soluzione utilizza tutte le 90 ore-macchina e tutte le 100 ore di lavoro. I prodotti \\(B\\) e \\(C\\) non vengono avviati né prodotti.",
